WEBVTT

00:09:58.436 --> 00:10:02.556
And they just kind of look
like white flowers floating in the wind.

00:10:02.596 --> 00:10:04.916
They’re actually really beautiful animals,

00:10:04.956 --> 00:10:06.676
and they’re living in, unbelievably,

00:10:06.676 --> 00:10:09.196
what we would class as being
extreme environments.

00:10:09.236 --> 00:10:12.276
They have an unpronounceable Latin name,

00:10:12.316 --> 00:10:15.916
which I maybe shouldn't try,
but it's Galatheanthemum.

00:10:15.916 --> 00:10:17.076
I've done it.

00:10:17.116 --> 00:10:20.596
(Laughter and applause)

00:10:20.636 --> 00:10:21.756
Thank you.

00:10:21.796 --> 00:10:23.716
(Applause)

00:10:23.756 --> 00:10:26.396
I'm not doing it again, though,
I got away with it once.

00:10:26.956 --> 00:10:29.596
So if you start to rethink
the visual imagery

00:10:29.636 --> 00:10:32.516
and the way in which
the deep sea is in reality